.TH "gen_wrapper" "3head" "2026\-10\-05" "TheCRatTime" "atexit"
.SH NAME
\fBgen_wrapper.\&h\fR \- generate wrappers.\&
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
You can generate wrappers, that will be do free with \fBAtExitHeader\fR.\& You can just
write \fBreturn\fR instead of \fBDoAtExit(somename); return\fR.\&
.PP
Need to define four macro:
.PP
\fBGEN_NAME\fR
.RS 4
Real function name.\&
.RE
.PP
\fBGEN_OUT\fR
.RS 4
Wrapper name.\&
.RE
.PP
\fBGEN_TYPE\fR
.RS 4
Type of return value.\&
.RE
.PP
\fBGEN_ARGS\fR
.RS 4
Arguments to wrapper.\&
.PP
To add one arg, write \fBGENARG(\fItype\fB, \fIname\fB)\fR where \fItype\fR is a
type of argument and \fBname\fR argument name.\&
.RE
.PP
\fBGEN_NOARGS\fR
.RS 4
Specify that function needs only one arg: \fBAtExitHeader\fR.\&
.PP
Cannot be defined with \fBGEN_ARGS\fR.\&
.RE
.PP
If you don't defined four macro, will be error.\&
You can disable errors with \fBATEXIT_DIS_ERROR\fR.\&
.PP
You can define \fBGEN_STATIC\fR for make function static.\&
.PP
.SH ERRORS
If you don't defined macro, will be error.\& This is can be
\fBDon't defined \fIGEN_OUT\fR, you need define \fIGEN_OUT\fR.\&
.PP
If you see \fBUndefine GEN_ARGS/GEN_NOARGS.\fR you defined \fBGEN_ARGS\fR and
\fBGEN_NOARGS\fR.\& Use \fB#undef\fR to fix it.\&
.PP
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
/* function: void RealAdd(AtExitHeader* atexit_h, int n1, int n2) */
#define GEN_NAME RealAdd /* function name */
#define GEN_OUT  Add /* Wrapper name */
#define GEN_TYPE void /* Return value */
#define GEN_ARGS GENARG(int, n1) GENARG(int, n2) /* You can write more*/
#include "gen_wrapper.h"

/* Wrapper will be automatically generated. */
.fi
.PP
.SH AUTHORS
Project and man\-page: TheCRatTime
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBatexit_do\fR(3), \fBatexit_defer\fR(3), \fBAtExitHeader\fR(3type)
